  "result": "The six-question quiz on O3 is written to `quizzes/0002.json`, with its answer key in `keys/0002.json`. I haven't answered it myself, so the key is unchecked against the stems.\n\nIt's called \"Picking a side or watching the keeper\". It has four multiple-choice items and two one-sentence short answers.\n- **Strategies:** what picking a side in advance means.\n- **Keeper types:** which strategy fits a keeper who dives early, and which fits one who waits.\n- **Trade-off:** the cost of watching the keeper and changing your aim late, and the risk of committing to a side.\n- **Your goal:** a plan that fits your goal of placing the ball in the corner with a controlled swing, which ties back to your planting and power habits.\n\nThe quiz is ahead of the lessons, because no lesson covers O3 yet. I built it from search-result summaries of a 2006 van der Kamp field study and a 2025 keeper-strategy modelling paper, not from reading the papers themselves. They were also the only sources found, so the keys may rest on weaker evidence than I'd like. I added a new misconception, M3 (you can watch the keeper and change your aim late at no cost), to `NOTES.md`.\n\nDo you want a lesson on this before you take the quiz?",
